>> title: Pot Roast, Slow Cooker
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, sunday dinner, braise, one-pot, slow cooker, crock pot
>> counters: The Slow Cooker
>> dish: pot-roast
>> kit: Slow Cooker
>> aka: yankee pot roast, hot beef commercial, hot beef sandwich, slow cooker pot roast, crockpot pot roast, crock pot roast
>> servings: 6
>> time: 8 hr 40 min
>> slack: forgiving — the potatoes give out first, and in a crock they were always going to be soft by the time the chuck is ready
>> washing-up: the slow cooker crock, the skillet, a cup to slake the cornstarch in, a plate to rest the roast on
>> keeps: 4 days — slice it cold and warm the slices in the gravy; the whole piece goes stringy warmed twice

Half the liquid the oven takes. Three cups going in is three cups plus what the vegetables give up coming out.

>> step: rub, both faces
Rub @beef chuck roast{4%lb}(1.8 kg) with @kosher salt{1%Tbs}, @black pepper{1%tsp}.

>> step: sear 12 min in a skillet, every face
Sear @&(~1)seasoned roast{} in @vegetable oil{2%Tbs} in a #skillet{} for ~sear{12%min}, turning it onto every face including the ends.

>> step: soften, deglaze the skillet clean
Soften @yellow onions{2%large}(sliced), @garlic{4%cloves}, @tomato paste{2%Tbs} in the same skillet with @&(~1)seared roast{}, then pour in @dry red wine{1/2%cup}(120 mL) and scrape until nothing is stuck to the base, which is the only place that flavour exists.

>> step: braise on low, 8 hr
Slow cook @&(~1)pot{} with @beef stock{1%cup}(240 mL), @thyme{4%sprigs}, @carrots{1%lb}(450 g; cut in 2-in lengths), @Yukon Gold potatoes{2%lb}(900 g; halved) in a #slow cooker{} on low for ~slow cook{8%hr}, lid on and left alone — every lift costs about twenty minutes of recovery.

>> step: thicken on high, lid off
Thicken @&(~1)pot roast{} on high with the lid off, stirring in @cornstarch{2%Tbs}(16 g; slaked in 2 Tbs cold water) for ~thicken{20%min}, the roast lifted out and resting under foil.
